---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { pages, site } from '../site';

const meta = pages['/about/'];
const article = 'https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/lazy-optimizer-why-we-need-stop-calling-ai-henard-gertzen-dnpef/';
---

<Base title={meta.title} description={meta.description} image="/og/about.png">
  <header class="page-head">
    <figure class="portrait-plate">
      <img src="/plates/portrait/henard.webp" alt="Henard Gertzen, smiling, in a white shirt and tie" width="400" height="400" />
      <img class="portrait-colour" src="/plates/portrait/henard-colour.webp" alt="" width="400" height="400" loading="lazy" />
    </figure>
    <p class="kicker">Full-stack developer <b>.NET</b> <b>Angular</b> <b>Claude Code</b></p>
    <h1 class="display">About Me</h1>
  </header>

  <article class="card">
    <div class="measure">
      <p class="dropcap">
        Secunda, South Africa, is where I live and work, as a full-stack developer. I help teams get coding agents to
        write code that fits their codebase, not just code that compiles.
      </p>
      <p>
        I wrote my first software in high school, as one of a handful of students in the first year group at my school
        to take IT, and built my first WordPress websites in holiday jobs. After school I worked as a hardware
        technician, keeping clients’ systems up to date.
      </p>
      <p>
        In 2021 I started a BSc in IT at North-West University in Potchefstroom. Alongside my studies I did freelance
        graphic and web design, and helped other students set up their computers, learn their software and get through
        their projects. In my final year I led our team on <a href="/projects/#share2teach">Share2Teach</a> as team
        lead, Scrum Master and head designer.
      </p>
      <p>
        After graduating I spent a few months as an intermediate full-stack developer at EziDev, then moved back to
        Secunda. Today I work remotely as a full-stack developer on .NET and Angular software, specialising in AI
        harnesses: the setup that makes coding agents work to a team’s standards.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside work I build <a href="/projects/#games">games with coding agents</a>, a point-of-sale system, and
        software for philosophy and theology. I think a lot about what AI actually is and the role agents play in our
        lives, and I’ve written about <a href={article}>why I’d rather call it a lazy optimizer than intelligent</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <dl class="readout">
      <div><dt>Based in</dt><dd>Secunda<small>South Africa, UTC+2</small></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Works on</dt><dd>.NET, Angular<small>and Claude Code</small></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Studied</dt><dd>BSc IT<small>North-West University</small></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Speaks</dt><dd>English<small>Afrikaans, some Dutch</small></dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="more">
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
      <a href={site.links.linkedin} rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
      <a href={site.links.github} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
      <a href="/contact/">What I do</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
